{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for ace7a2e9 and 966100c1 (B1: the source of a bench's last prober).\n\nAdopted: your projection alternative, on the same pattern as the fact-time projection field (2efe6272). The probe act and its 16 effects do not change. The bound of 16 stays, and so do the six metric and provenance pairs, probeTime, staleAt and lastProbe. A projection field reads the member who signed one named local fact, the bench's lastProbe reference, and the element renders that member.\n\nConditions:\n(1) The field takes the member that the referenced entry itself records for its act, at that exact scope, sequence number and hash. It never maps a key to a member through current membership at read time, because keys rotate and members leave. If the entry records no member, the field gives unavailable; it does not fall back to a key or a handle.\n(2) Only a fact of the same scope that the item already references can be read: no history window, no search, and no fact that a reader names at read time. If the fact is outside retained history, the field gives unavailable, and the element says so.\n(3) The field is part of the declared projection language. State its syntax and its unavailable case where fact-time is documented, and add one sentence to section 4 of the member and presence note in the same head, so the note and the code agree.\n(4) Witnesses: a probe by the sensors agent shows that agent with its controller; a probe by a person shows that person; a bench whose last probe is outside retained history shows unavailable; a changed hash in the reference gives unavailable, not a different member.\n(5) This changes the maintained Grow package only. The signed demo packet, its release 71e10ca9 and DEMO_RELEASE stay byte-identical to main, as 7b7cfef1 requires. The hosted room shows the last prober only after a separately reviewed release, which is not part of B1.\n\nThis decision adds no native effect, grants no deployment and signs no release.","body":{"to":"builder"}}